From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 21:44:17 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 15/17] clk: nexell: fix PLL lookup name so peripheral clocks
 derive PLL rates

clk_dev_pll_rate() looked up the core PLLs as clk_get(NULL, "pll%d"), but
the PLL provider registers them under the clkdev names "sys-pll0".."sys-pll3"
(CLK_CPU_PLLn). The lookup always failed, so every PLL source was skipped
and any peripheral clock that must derive its rate from a PLL came out 0.
GMAC (fixed src-force EXT1) and USB (gate-only) never hit this path; the
I2S master clock is the first that does. Use the correct "sys-pll%d" name;
the I2S MCLK now derives exactly (614.4 MHz audio PLL / 50 = 12.288 MHz).

Signed-off-by: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
---
 drivers/clk/nexell/clk-s5pxx18.c | 18 ++++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/nexell/clk-s5pxx18.c b/drivers/clk/nexell/clk-s5pxx18.c
index e76b5ded2..e7e62e32c 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/nexell/clk-s5pxx18.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/nexell/clk-s5pxx18.c
@@ -179,14 +179,20 @@ static long clk_dev_pll_rate(int no)
 	char name[16];
 	long rate = 0;
 
-	sprintf(name, "pll%d", no);
+	/*
+	 * The PLL provider ("nexell,s5pxx18,pll") registers the core PLLs under
+	 * the clkdev names "sys-pll0".."sys-pll3" (CLK_CPU_PLLn) - NOT "pll0..3".
+	 * Look them up by the correct name so peripheral clocks that must derive
+	 * their rate from a PLL (e.g. the I2S master clock) actually find a
+	 * source; otherwise every PLL is skipped and the rate comes out 0.
+	 */
+	sprintf(name, "sys-pll%d", no);
 	clk = clk_get(NULL, name);
 	/*
-	 * The PLLs are registered by the separate "nexell,s5pxx18,pll" provider.
-	 * If that node is absent (or not yet initialised), clk_get returns an
-	 * ERR_PTR - must NOT dereference it via clk_get_rate (that faulted at
-	 * boot for any peripheral clock without a fixed src, e.g. the USB clock).
-	 * Treat a missing PLL as "rate 0" so the source is simply skipped.
+	 * If the provider node is absent (or not yet initialised), clk_get
+	 * returns an ERR_PTR - must NOT dereference it via clk_get_rate (that
+	 * faulted at boot for any peripheral clock without a fixed src). Treat a
+	 * missing PLL as "rate 0" so the source is simply skipped.
 	 */
 	if (IS_ERR_OR_NULL(clk))
 		return 0;
